-{"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-44", "title": "[P2] --repair-events re-encodes each renumbered event through map[string]any and silently mutates NON-id fields (ints >2^53 round, double spaces collapse inside string values, keys reorder) — README promises 'every other field untouched'", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 25 (tick boardctl-dogfood-2026-10-23-10-52-34), reproduced at HEAD 900b7b5 and on the RELEASED v0.1.11 binary on a fresh bunker box. Fixture events.jsonl (3 events, ids 10,9,11; the 9 descends) with a renumbered line carrying 'detail':'cmd: rsync -a  /x  /y', 'title':'fix  double  spaces', 'tick_number':9007199254740993, keys z_first before a_last. After `boardctl normalize-board --repair-events --apply` the line reads { \"a_last\": \"z\", ..., \"detail\": \"cmd: rsync -a /x /y\", ..., \"id\": 11, ..., \"tick_number\": 9007199254740992, ..., \"title\": \"fix double spaces\", \"z_first\": \"a\" } — the double spaces inside TWO string VALUES were collapsed (the recorded command and the title no longer match what was written), the 2^53+1 integer was rounded DOWN to 2^53, and key order was rewritten alphabetically. LIVE evidence: a scratch copy of the real task-router board (700 events, 473 descending ids) repaired with --apply → exactly 1 of the 473 renumbered events lost non-id bytes (events.jsonl line 691, its detail JSON body re-indented 2→1 spaces: '\"tick_id\": ...' went from '\\n  \"' to '\\n \"'). Code: internal/board/repair_events.go:224-250 renumberEventID unmarshals into map[string]any (float64 for every number, sorted keys on re-marshal) and then runs bytes.ReplaceAll(out, []byte('  '), []byte(' ')) over the WHOLE re-encoded line, which reaches inside string values. This contradicts README ~line 878 ('leaves every other field on the event untouched') and the file's own header comment (repair_events.go:15 'preserve every field except \"id\"'). Fix direction: surgical id-only byte rewrite on the raw line (locate the id token) or, at minimum, decode with json.Decoder+UseNumber and drop the global double-space normalization.", "created_at": "2026-10-23T11:23:17Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T11:23:17Z", "created_by": "dogfood-boardctl-run25", "acceptance_criteria": "1) On a fixture where a descending event carries 'title':'fix  double  spaces', 'detail':'cmd: rsync -a  /x  /y', 'tick_number':9007199254740993 and a deliberately non-alphabetical key order, `normalize-board --repair-events --apply` leaves every one of those values and the key order byte-identical — only the id token changes (prove with a byte diff of the line). 2) A regression test in internal/board covers all three shapes (double-space string, >2^53 integer, key order) and fails on the current implementation. 3) Re-running the real-board repair on a copy of task-router's board yields ZERO non-id diffs when old and new events are compared field-by-field (run 25's checker printed 1). 4) `go test ./...` exits 0.", "capability_tags": [], "complexity": 3, "depends_on": [], "foreman_note": null, "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "17ce981adb436ef60e957b399ca3e74b3cbeb8c7577b26a55a688fd0b6ca1bca"}}
